x86_64-linux  cxx1 emits the C1 form of each nested class's constructor (Holder<T>::Box, Scaled<T,N>::In, Tag<T>::type, Outer<T>::Mid) beside the C2 where clang emits only the C2 it calls - the inline-constructor difference qualified-functional-cast.nonames records; the probe's nested classes must define their constructors inside, the shape slice 3v reads. x86_64-windows and arm64-darwin agree on every name.
